  <h2 id="install">Install</h2>
  <p>Ravenburst runs on Windows 10 and 11, macOS 13 or later, and 64-bit Linux. Installers will be on the <a href="/download">Download page</a> at launch.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Windows:</strong> run the <code>.exe</code> installer.</li>
    <li><strong>macOS:</strong> open the <code>.dmg</code> and drag Ravenburst to Applications.</li>
    <li><strong>Linux:</strong> make the <code>.AppImage</code> file executable and run it.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="trial">Your free trial</h2>
  <p>The first time Ravenburst opens with an internet connection, it starts a <strong>7-day free trial</strong> on that computer. There's no account to create and no card to enter. A bar at the top of the window counts down the days.</p>
  <p>If the computer is offline the first time, the bar says <em>Connect to the internet once to start your free trial</em>. You can write in the meantime; the trial starts the next time Ravenburst can reach the internet.</p>
  <p>See <a href="/docs/license">License &amp; Activation</a> for what changes when the trial ends.</p>

  <h2 id="project">Create a project</h2>
  <p>A project holds one piece of work: a novel, a screenplay, a paper. Everything in it (chapters, notes, character sheets, research, snapshots) is saved in a single <code>.ravenburst</code> file.</p>
  <ol>
    <li>Choose <span class="menu">File → New Project…</span> (<kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>N</kbd>), or <strong>New Project</strong> on the start screen.</li>
    <li>Choose a name and a place to save it. Ravenburst suggests <code>Documents/Ravenburst</code>. Names can use letters, numbers, spaces, hyphens and underscores.</li>
    <li>Pick a <strong>project type</strong>, for example Novel, Screenplay or Academic Paper (APA 7th). See <a href="/docs/project-templates">Project Templates</a> for all 15.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>Ravenburst sets the project up for that kind of work: a first chapter and scene, front matter pages for the formats you're likely to export, and starter templates.</p>

  <h2 id="window">The window</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Navigator</strong> (left): every part of your project, from the manuscript to your trash. Click anything to open it. See <a href="/docs/navigator">Navigator &amp; Structure</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Editor</strong> (centre): where you write, with the <strong>Format Bar</strong> above it. See <a href="/docs/editor">The Editor</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Inspector</strong> (right): details of the selected document: its status, word target, label colour and synopsis. With nothing selected it shows <strong>Project Settings</strong>.</li>
    <li><strong>Status bar</strong> (bottom): zoom, spellcheck, word counts, save status, backup status and the theme.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Show or hide any of these from <span class="menu">View → Show / Hide</span>. To put the Navigator on the right, use <span class="menu">Window → Move Navigator Right</span>.</p>

  <h2 id="saving">Saving</h2>
  <p>Ravenburst saves by itself a few seconds after you stop typing (3 seconds unless you change it in <a href="/docs/preferences">Preferences</a>). The status bar shows <em>Saved</em>, <em>Saving…</em> or <em>Unsaved changes</em>. <span class="menu">File → Save</span> (<kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>S</kbd>) saves at once.</p>
  <p>When you open Ravenburst again, it reopens the project and document you were last working on.</p>

